From: ANGI build integration
Subject: [PATCH] Retain safe open fallback when toolchain headers lack openat2

The appliance kernel is new enough for openat2, but some external toolchains
use older syscall headers. On x86-64 use the Linux syscall table's openat2
number when the headers lack it. Retain bubblewrap's safe fallback for other
targets with older headers. Sandbox restrictions remain enabled.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/safe_openat.c
+++ b/safe_openat.c
@@ -32,7 +32,12 @@
 
 bool opt_force_openat_fallback = false;
 
-#if ASSUMED_KERNEL < BWRAP_KERNEL_VERSION (5, 6, 0)
+/* arch/x86/entry/syscalls/syscall_64.tbl */
+#if !defined(__NR_openat2) && defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__ILP32__)
+#  define __NR_openat2 437
+#endif
+
+#if ASSUMED_KERNEL < BWRAP_KERNEL_VERSION (5, 6, 0) || !defined(__NR_openat2)
 #  define USE_OPENAT_FALLBACK 1
 #else
 #  define USE_OPENAT_FALLBACK 0
